sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RN as gents renewal: extend the lease of request r
    participant AP as gents appender: append a segment for r
    participant IL as client: latch an interrupt on r
    participant D as defradb.rs worker and regolith

    RN->>D: get_parts(r, state, generation, expiry)
    AP->>D: get_parts(r, state, generation)
    IL->>D: merge(r, operand touching interrupt only)
    RN->>D: merge(r, operand touching expiry)
    AP->>D: create segment, append(journal)
    IL->>D: commit
    D-->>IL: committed
    RN->>D: commit
    D-->>RN: committed: the interrupt touched a part renewal did not read
    AP->>D: commit
    alt after gents decides on generation, not on the expiry deadline
        D-->>AP: committed: renewal touched expiry, a part the appender did not read
    else with gents' current lease model, the appender also reads expiry
        D-->>AP: Conflict: mine ReadParts, theirs Merge on expiry
        Note over AP: a race gents' own model requires today, removable by its lease change
    end
